# The working copy of this repo IS what the SFTP watcher uploads to production.
# Never let git rewrite line endings on checkout -- a checkout that changed them
# would change the bytes running in production.
#
# This repo is NOT uniformly CRLF, despite what this file used to claim. Endings
# are mixed FILE BY FILE -- ServerBuilder.php is pure CRLF, server_api.php and
# BaseFunctions.php are pure LF -- so any script that rewrites a file must detect
# that file's own ending rather than assume the repo's.
#
# `-text` alone was not enough: core.autocrlf was still `true`, so 30 files had
# been checked out converted to CRLF while their blobs stayed LF, and git's stat
# cache reported the repo clean the whole time. autocrlf is now `false` locally in
# all three repos and the index was renormalized to the working bytes on
# 2026-09-16, so what is committed is finally what production runs. Do not set
# autocrlf back to true here.
#
# Note that `git status` being clean does not by itself prove the index matches
# the bytes on disk; `git hash-object <file>` against `git ls-files -s <file>` does.
* -text
